## Plan
I'll rename the public type in one pass and leave the storage format alone, so existing sessions keep opening.

1. Rename the type in `src/session/store.rs`.
2. Update the **14 call sites** across five files, including the ones behind `#[cfg(test)]`, which are easy to miss because they only compile under `cargo test`.
3. Run `cargo test --locked` and `cargo clippy`.

Things I will not touch:
- the JSON field names on disk
- public CLI flags
  - `--resume` keeps its current spelling
  - `--session` stays an alias

> The file format is versioned by `format: 3`; renaming the Rust type does not change what gets written.

```rust
pub struct SessionLedger {
    dir: PathBuf,
    // Opened lazily; see open().
    format: u32,
}

fn open(dir: &Path) -> io::Result<SessionLedger> {
    let format = 3;
    Ok(SessionLedger { dir: dir.into(), format })
}
```

---

Background on the naming: see [the ADR](https://example.dev/adr/0007) for why "ledger" fits an append-only log. Done ✓ 👍🏽

